/P 92 0 R
/E (To effectively address these variances, managers can examine specific metrics such as Covers, Per Person Average, and the number of hours utilized in both the front of house and back of house operations, along with the blended wage. Each of these elements offers insights into the operational nuances that may be impacting overall performance. It's important to recognize that each cause of variance may require a different solution; mistakenly treating them all as mere labor issues can lead to misguided decisions and the cutting of essential resources. By taking a detailed, analytical approach to evaluating these variances, management can implement targeted strategies that truly address the root causes and ultimately enhance overall efficiency and performance.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
