/E (Learning Management Systems \(LMS\) have revolutionized the way operators train their staff, providing a structured and efficient alternative to traditional training methods. With features that allow for the creation of customized training materials, testing and scoring capabilities, and the automatic assignment of learning modules, LMS platforms not only streamline the training process but also allow operators to track staff progress in real-time. This enhanced visibility into employee development is crucial for ensuring that team members acquire the essential skills and knowledge necessary for success. However, the financial commitment required for these systems can be a significant hurdle, with costs ranging from $400 to $3,000 per month for a restaurant employing around 50 staff. Given the multitude of technology solutions that operators must integrate to maintain competitiveness, investing in comprehensive training often falls by the wayside.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [0]
